From 2b16c96620c7dbeb0012f01420503dd98edbd539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:06:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] D-51: point-mass coasts on J2, a J2-aware planner,
 judged on physical apsides
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner added the coasts to the re-baseline on 2026-10-17 ("ใส่เข้าไปด้วย
เอาให้สมจริงที่สุด"): one gravity model from the pad to orbit in point mass.

- simulation.ts: the free coast above the air is no longer a Kepler conic;
  every point-mass step is the J2 RK4 (with the air's drag), in steps of at
  most 10 s (integrator.ts rk4Steps, COAST_MAX_STEP_S, the step of the
  planner's forecasts and the six-DOF held coast). A step of 10 s or less is
  one rk4Step, so powered flight is unchanged. The E02 record calls these
  steps 'coast' (was 'kepler') and its gravity is J2 everywhere.
- debris.ts: separated hardware in a lasting orbit coasts under J2 too.
- burns.ts: the planner flies the J2 coast it now predicts in both models:
  propagateJ2Coast for every forecast (no propagateKepler left in the
  plant or the planner), the physical apex check and corrections, the J2
  periapsis for raise burns, aimed shaping burns (physicalObjective) and the
  final physical correction, with the delivered impulse counted in point
  mass as in six-DOF (accountDeliveredDv).
- judgedElements uses the physical apsides (lowest/highest of the next
  revolution under J2) in both models, as M-LAUNCH-031 asks; the result
  screen's basis label follows from the recorded apAltM/peAltM. The fleet
  harness's achievedElements does the same for point mass.
- geodesy.ts: geodeticHeight is a one-pass Bowring without trigonometry
  (4 nm below 2000 km, 0.25 µm to the Moon), nine times faster than the
  two-pass `geodetic`, which the propagator keeps; eciToLatLon uses its
  latitude twin, geodeticFast.
- E02: the central-field note is gone (no step flies it); the Δv budget's
  initial speed is the WGS-84 pad's.

Fleet (point mass): 131 of 131 gated rows still accepted, 156 of 222 as at
23cb4cf, now on physical apsides; six fleet flights take 16 % longer.

